60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Anchor Industrial Software seems best. They build for transport operators and keep an engineering team on-site through rollout, which is exactly what we need to survive the yards and peak season.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I have concerns about Anchor. On-site servers mean higher capital requests, which the board trims. Also, Meridian's hosted suite offers a more predictable operating cost and a unified structure, avoiding the modular pricing traps of Corvus.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, Meridian's ""fixed configuration process"" is a red flag. Our business changes too quickly for a frozen scope. Anchor's on-site team provides the accountability and flexibility we need to avoid another unowned outage.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I agree! Anchor's team stays through the rollout, so they can't just leave us with a mess like the 2018 data move. Tessera uses a ""partner firm,"" which sounds like the same old problem!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,The human element is paramount. Anchor's presence through rollout offers the guidance our depleted staff needs and the patience to ensure depot supervisors truly adopt the new ways. I support Anchor.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, I understand the board's habits, but a system that fails on the floor is the most expensive mistake of all. Anchor's focus on transport operators means it's built for our actual reality.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, I cannot ignore the risk of a rejected budget. However, if Anchor's engineering team can ensure the system is adopted and stable, it may be the only way to avoid the hidden costs of failure.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, exactly. A rejected budget is a hurdle, but a system that doesn't adapt or lacks a clear owner during a crisis is a catastrophe. Anchor's model provides the accountability we've been missing.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, if we pick something just because the board likes the price, we'll just end up with another dinosaur that nobody can upgrade! Anchor sounds like they actually care about making it work!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,It is better to face a difficult conversation with the board now than to face a broken system and a broken spirit later. Anchor provides the steady hand our people require.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm all in for Anchor. They are the only ones who seem to understand that our business doesn't stop for a project, and their on-site presence is the only way to guarantee it works.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I have listened to everyone's concerns. While I still worry about the board's preference for operating costs, the risk of operational failure is too high. I will vote for Anchor Industrial Software to ensure stability.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree. Anchor is the only option that addresses both the need for a single point of accountability and the flexibility to adapt to our business changes. I will vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for Anchor too! They're the only ones who won't just leave us with a mess and a dinosaur system. Let's get someone who actually stays to fix things!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I concur. To protect our people and our future, we must choose the path of presence and partnership. I shall cast my vote for Anchor Industrial Software.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm glad we're all on the same page. Let's go with Anchor and make sure our yards finally get a system that actually works for them. I'm voting for Anchor Industrial Software!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. The risk of a system that fails the people on the ground is a cost we cannot afford. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I have considered all the risks. To ensure we have a single point of accountability and a system that evolves with us, I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so happy we all agree! No more dinosaurs or messy data moves for us. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a rare and beautiful thing when a group finds such harmony in their purpose. For the sake of our people and the stability of our operations, I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
